# shell: both
# work: home
# PVK-038/FS-046: the Delete key, which this shell did not have at all.  What
# it means depends on where the item is: a move that can be undone where there
# is a Trash, and a deletion when Shift says the user has decided.
note FS-046: Delete asks first, and says what cannot be taken back
click-row 1
wait 3
key Delete
wait 5
expect-alert cannot be reverted
note Escape is the Cancel button: the file is still where it was
key Escape
wait 20
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/a.txt
note and 'm' is Move to Trash, which is what the question offers instead
key Delete
wait 5
expect-alert cannot be reverted
key m
wait 30
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/a.txt
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/a.txt
note Shift+Delete is final, and says so -- no question, because Shift IS the
note answer to it
click-row 1
wait 3
key Delete shift
wait 30
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/b.txt
note and it is not in the Trash either, which is the whole difference
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/b.txt
note 'd' takes the third way out: gone, without passing through the Trash
click-row 1
wait 3
key Delete
wait 5
expect-alert cannot be reverted
key d
wait 30
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/c.txt
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/c.txt
quit
